==Strategy==
==='''Chapter 1'''===
The entire stage is just aliens so just use anti alien debuffers, including [[Surfer Cat (Super Rare Cat)|Seafarer cat]] or [[Psychocat (Rare Cat)|Psychocat]]. If you really don't want to worry about it, bring [[Fencer Cat (Super Rare Cat)|Kendo Cat/The Kitty of Liberty]] to break Gregory's barrier.

==='''Chapter 2'''===
Lure the Kid Tappa near your base, and start using it to stack [[Surfer Cat (Super Rare Cat)|Seafarers]] along with any spammable attackers. Once you're done, deploy a high damage attacker like [[Hip Hop Cat (Super Rare Cat)|Can Can Cat]] or [[Wheel Cat (Rare Cat)|Chill Cat]] to break the Tappa's barrier, and the rest of the stage should play itself.

==='''Chapter 3'''===
Use the same strategy as before, and it will work nonetheless. But since there are Mesocosmocyclones in the stage, use their warps to cheese the stage somewhat easily.

Alternatively, you can cheese the stage: with strong rushers such as [[Ancient Egg: N101 (Rare Cat)|Courier Cat]], [[Hip Hop Cat (Super Rare Cat)|Can Can Cat]], and [[Express Cat (Super Rare Cat)|Maglev Cat]], you can rush the stage before Mesocosmocyclones can cause you any trouble. To do this, you must send out your units fast and push to the base before Kid Tappa can slow you down or stop your momentum. You should also set aside some slots for unit trait combos (attack/speed/defense).

